    { "term": "Ndongo and Matamba", "matchText": "Ndongo and Matamba", "type": "place", "definition": "Two neighboring kingdoms in seventeenth-century Angola ruled by Queen Njinga, who fought the Portuguese for nearly four decades. She built Matamba into a powerful state that outlasted her and became a symbol of African resistance to European conquest." },
