    { "term": "French abolition of slavery", "matchText": "abolition of slavery", "type": "event", "definition": "In 1794, pressed by the unstoppable revolt in Saint-Domingue and by the logic of its own revolution, the French Republic declared the abolition of slavery in all its colonies — the first time a great power formally took the side of the enslaved's freedom. Napoleon would try to reverse it." },
