    { "term": "American Civil War", "matchText": "American Civil War", "type": "event", "definition": "The 1861–1865 war between the slaveholding South and the free North, fought ultimately over the existence and expansion of slavery. It was the bloodiest war in American history, and it was what finally ended slavery in the United States." },
    { "term": "Abraham Lincoln", "matchText": "Abraham Lincoln", "type": "person", "definition": "President of the United States during the Civil War. In 1863 he issued the Emancipation Proclamation, declaring the enslaved in the rebelling Confederate states free and turning the war into a struggle over slavery itself." },
