    { "term": "Law of the Free Womb", "matchText": "Law of the Free Womb", "type": "event", "definition": "An 1871 Brazilian law declaring that children thereafter born to enslaved women would be free — though only after years of labor for their mother's owner. A gradualist measure meant to let slavery die out slowly rather than end at a stroke." },
