    { "term": "Trans-Atlantic Slave Trade Database", "matchText": "Trans-Atlantic Slave Trade Database", "type": "concept", "definition": "A decades-long scholarly project that reconstructed the Atlantic slave trade voyage by voyage from surviving shipping records — the source of the headline figures of roughly 12.5 million Africans embarked and 10.7 million surviving to land across some 36,000 documented voyages. The numbers are best estimates, and almost certainly a floor." },
